AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::setTreasuryInterestBps(uint256)
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount and preserve the current share
├── when the new share exceeds the full allocation
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput and preserve the current share
├── when the new share is within the allowed range
│   ├── it should update treasuryInterestBps and emit SetTreasuryInterestBps with old and new values
│   ├── it should allow zero and full treasury allocations
│   ├── when the new share equals the current share
│   │   └── it should still emit SetTreasuryInterestBps
│   └── when fees are already outstanding
│       ├── it should not accrue interest mint tokens or change market accounting
│       └── it should apply the new share when those fees are subsequently claimed
└── when the market is paused or frozen
    └── it should remain callable by the owner
